course: dictionary
lesson: 15290
title: Sitcom
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A sitcom is a funny show on TV or radio. The word is short for «situation comedy». The same characters appear in every episode, and the jokes come from everyday life, like a family arguing about who does the washing-up.
explain: «We watched a sitcom about a family who lived next door to a grumpy neighbour.» The clues are funny show and the same family: a sitcom is a series, not a one-off film. Ask yourself: do the same people come back each week? If they do, it is probably a sitcom.
explain: «The sitcom characters always got into trouble at school.» Characters are the people in the show. Once you know a sitcom is a funny series, you can predict that its stories will be about ordinary things, not space or dragons.
fact: A sitcom is a funny TV or radio series.
fact: «Sitcom» is short for «situation comedy».
fact: A sitcom uses the same characters in every episode.
fact: Many sitcoms show everyday situations, like a family, or friends at work.
fact: A «laugh track» is a recording of people laughing, often added to a sitcom.
exercise: «We watched a funny sitcom about a family with five noisy children.» What is a sitcom? | *A funny TV or radio series about the same characters | A book of poems about the sea | A serious news report about the weather | A long walk in the countryside
exercise: «Sitcom» is short for two words. Which two words? | *situation comedy | single corner | sit down and cook | story collection
exercise: «The sitcom characters always got into trouble at school.» What are the characters? | The laugh track | The TV remote | *The people in the show | The scenery behind the actors
test: «My favourite sitcom is on every Thursday night.» What does sitcom mean here? | A news programme about the weather | A sad film about one night | A kind of sport | *A funny series with the same characters
test: What is the short form of «situation comedy»? | situ | sitter | *sitcom | comedian
exam: «The sitcom had a laugh track, so we heard people laughing at every joke.» What is a laugh track? | *A recording of laughter added to a show | A type of bicycle | A kind of cooking pot | A track for running races
